## Project identity
- **Repo:** `github.com/fleXRPL/signal`
- **Live site:** `flexrpl.github.io/signal`
- **Purpose:** Personal daily + weekly political intelligence pipeline. Also a public reference repo showing how to build a production-quality LLM pipeline. Not a commercial product.
- **Owner:** garotconklin (solo developer)

## Stack
- Python 3.14, SQLite, launchd (macOS scheduling)
- LLM: Claude Code CLI (`claude -p`) — default and required for scheduled runs
- LLM alt: Ollama (`qwen2.5:14b`) — interactive/manual only, never in launchd
- Publishing: GitHub Pages + GitHub Actions
- Analytics: GA4 (`G-58PDJM14L7`)

## Code standards
- Senior-level production Python: passes linting, security, efficiency
- Minimum Viable Product first — deliver working before polishing
- No comments that narrate what code does — only explain non-obvious intent
- All new features on a feature branch; merge to main when stable
- SonarQube Cloud integration — resolve warnings before declaring done

## Non-negotiables
- NEVER run Ollama from launchd — causes Metal GPU kernel panics on macOS
- NEVER push to main from a feature branch during a launchd run (scripts must `git checkout main` first)
- NEVER commit `signal.db`, `*.log`, `.env`, or `secrets.yaml`
